# Godwall subsystem — Tor daemon configuration (torrc)
#
# PROVENANCE / LICENCE. The option set and defaults mirror InviZible Pro's
# preferences_tor (github.com/Gedsh/InviZible, GPL-3.0). Tor itself is
# © The Tor Project, BSD-3-Clause. This is configuration derived from a study of
# the donor's option surface, not copied Kotlin. A NOTICE entry for the Tor
# binary + InviZible-derived config is required before this ships — see
# .octo/parallel/WP-4/output.md.
#
# This file is a COMPLETE, working default. Configuring the backend is not the
# user's job (charter rule C). It is seeded into the prefix ONCE with
# overwrite=false, so an Advanced surface's raw edit survives a restart.
# TorDaemonSettings.renderTorrc() reproduces this CONFIGURATION (same directives
# and values) for the default settings and regenerates it when a preference
# changes; the regenerated form is machine-authored and drops these teaching
# comments. The two are kept semantically in lock-step, not byte-identical.
#
# Absolute paths against the fixed prefix /data/local/tmp/godwall (= Bootstrap.PREFIX).
# Nothing here runs until the `tor` ELF is present at usr/bin/tor. When the binary
# is absent the Anonymity capability reports ABSENT and this config is inert; it is
# never a claim that Tor is running.

# The daemon MUST stay in the foreground. The Supervisor tracks the pid the launch
# shell reported; RunAsDaemon 1 would double-fork and detach from that pid, leaving
# a live tor nothing is supervising. This is a contract from ServiceSpec, not taste.
RunAsDaemon 0

DataDirectory /data/local/tmp/godwall/home/tor
Log notice file /data/local/tmp/godwall/logs/tor-notice.log

# GeoIP tables. Required for country-code node selection (Exit/Entry/Exclude
# Nodes). Shipped by the InviZible app_data tree, which is an OPEN payload
# (docs/DONOR-ASSETS.md) — when these files are absent tor still runs and only
# by-country node selection is inert. Anonymity gates those specific controls on
# the presence of these files rather than letting them silently no-op.
GeoIPFile /data/local/tmp/godwall/usr/etc/tor/geoip
GeoIPv6File /data/local/tmp/godwall/usr/etc/tor/geoip6

# Transparent-proxy address mapping (preferences_tor > "Virtual Addr Network").
VirtualAddrNetworkIPv4 10.192.0.0/10
AutomapHostsOnResolve 1

# ── Common settings (preferences_tor > "Common settings") — donor defaults ─────
HardwareAccel 1
AvoidDiskWrites 1
ConnectionPadding 1
ReducedConnectionPadding 1
NewCircuitPeriod 30
MaxCircuitDirtiness 600
DormantClientTimeout 15 minutes
DormantCanceledByStartup 1
EnforceDistinctSubnets 1
ClientUseIPv4 1
ClientUseIPv6 1
# FascistFirewall — off by default (Enable to keep to firewalled 80/443 ORs).
# TrackHostExits — off by default.

# ── Listeners (preferences_tor > "Proxy") — donor ports ────────────────────────
# SOCKSPort keeps Tor's default per-SOCKS-auth stream isolation on: "Isolate By
# UID" is realised by the datapath handing each app distinct SOCKS credentials.
# Isolate-by-dest-addr / dest-port are off by default and appended by the renderer.
SOCKSPort 9050
TransPort 9040
DNSPort 5400
# HTTPTunnelPort 8118            — Enable HTTP Tunnel: off by default.
# Socks5Proxy 127.0.0.1:1080    — Enable output SOCKS5 proxy: off by default.

# Control port for "New Tor identity" (NEWNYM). Cookie auth: tor writes
# control_auth_cookie into DataDirectory as uid 2000; TorControl reads it through
# the privileged shell, authenticates, and issues SIGNAL NEWNYM. Loopback only.
ControlPort 9051
CookieAuthentication 1

# ── Bridges (preferences_fast > "Bridges") ─────────────────────────────────────
# Off by default: tor connects directly. The pluggable-transport lines are
# TEMPLATES and stay commented because their PT binaries (obfs4proxy,
# snowflake-client) are SEPARATE payloads that are not in this build
# (docs/DONOR-ASSETS.md). TorBridges.renderTorrcLines() emits the exact transport
# the user selects, and ONLY when its PT binary is present at the path shown, so
# tor is never told to exec a transport that is not there.
#UseBridges 1
#ClientTransportPlugin obfs4,meek_lite exec /data/local/tmp/godwall/usr/bin/obfs4proxy
#ClientTransportPlugin snowflake exec /data/local/tmp/godwall/usr/bin/snowflake-client
#Bridge obfs4 <ip>:<port> <fingerprint> cert=<cert> iat-mode=0
